% Typed local JSON/Markdown results and CLI.
Commands: inventory, prepare, check, doctor; JSON is stable schema version 1.
<vocabulary>
trusted: part of the immutable pinned image or an independently human-reviewed challenge specification.
untrusted: caller-provided source, compiled data, logs or metaprograms, never authority for the verdict.
invalid: bytes that fail UTF-8 decoding or a value failing the documented schema.
unsafe: a path that contains Docker mount delimiters or resolves through symlinks.
authorized: explicitly selected by the human in the invoking agent session.
</vocabulary>
<contract_rules>
R-401 (MUST): separate model_proof_status, source_correspondence_status and specification_review_status. No universal verified badge.
R-402 (MUST): distinguish rejected proof/export/kernel checks from timeout, output limit, malformed input, missing prerequisites and other errors; an unproved property is not a proven source bug.
R-403 (MUST): include reproducible source snapshot hashes, source mappings, assumptions, expected obligations, image/toolchain identity, coverage and action-oriented findings.
R-404 (MUST): write reports only to fresh private workspaces and fail on overwrite/symlink/public-tree output risks. Do not publish automatically.
R-405 (MUST): expose library functions and stable CLI JSON without embedding a provider or claiming automatic source-to-Lean translation.
</contract_rules>
